# One line ending everywhere, stored and checked out as LF.
#
# Why this file exists: this repo is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf=true,
# so tracked files arrive in the working tree as CRLF — but the generators
# (scripts/generate-*.mjs, and the trust-layer patch step in particular) write
# their output with bare \n. The result was mixed-EOL files, so `git status`
# reported ~40 hand-authored pages as modified after every single build even
# though not one byte of content had changed. That is FINDINGS.md #3, and it
# made "is the tree clean?" useless as a signal — you could not tell a real
# edit from build noise without hashing CR-stripped content by hand.
#
# Normalizing to LF in the repository ends that permanently: the generators'
# output and the checked-out file now agree.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never normalized, never diffed as text.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.ico  binary
*.svg  text eol=lf
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.eot   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.zip   binary
